00:55:55,350 --> 00:55:59,350
And whichever order I hit these two.

585
00:55:59,350 --> 00:56:01,350
So those two are impossible.

586
00:56:01,350 --> 00:56:10,090
So that's the idea of sequential consistency, that there's some very large number but of possible outputs

587
00:56:10,090 --> 00:56:15,570
of a program, but in any case, they can't violate the ordering and

588
00:56:15,590 --> 00:56:17,590
by the individual threads.

589
00:56:17,590 --> 00:56:23,230
So you'd say, okay, duh, that seems like pretty obvious thing.

